values ('f4a5b6c7-8d9e-4a14-9b34-4c5d6e7f8a44', 'medical-anthropology', 'Medical Anthropology', 'Medical Anthropology examines health, illness, healing, suffering, and care as biological, cultural, political, economic, ecological, and moral phenomena. Students learn to analyze clinical systems, public health programs, epidemics, mental health, reproduction, disability, technology, and global health through ethnographic and biocultural methods.');

